    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting the favorable matchup against Bailey Ober. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.18) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.01) lead the charge as our strongest plays, benefiting significantly from the matchup against a high xERA arm and prime spots in the batting order. **Miguel Vargas** (62.46) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) are also high-leverage starts today; both capitalize on the exploitable pitching profile of Ober, with **Antonacci** specifically gaining a massive boost from his projected leadoff spot. While **Kyle Tucker** (66.85) faces a tougher matchup against Andrew Alvarez, his elite base production maintains his status as a locked-in core piece for the Waves today.\n\nDeciding between our bottom-tier outfielders and utility options proved difficult, with **Coby Mayo** (56.06) narrowly edging out **Jackson Merrill** (55.37) for the final utility spot. The decision came down to **Mayo**\u2019s superior dynamic platoon advantage against the lefty Tolle, which outweighed the high-volume base production of **Merrill**. We are keeping a close eye on **Nasim Nunez** (53.34); while his offensive projection is marginal, his utility as a speed threat against a pitcher with slow delivery mechanics keeps him in the starting nine to hunt for that scarce SB category. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given several high-end arms on the schedule. We are wary of **Wade Meckler** (40.30), whose start against Skenes is purely defensive; his floor is dangerously low due to the elite nature of the opposing pitcher. We continue to monitor the status of our injured core, including **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson**, all of whom remain on the IL. As we look toward the bench, depth pieces like **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Tommy White**, **Curtis Mead**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara** are ready to rotate in should any of our \"Lineup Pending\" players, specifically **Nasim Nunez**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Kyle Tucker**, or **Sam Antonacci**, fail to crack their respective official lineups.",
